{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1021856-scale-and-sensory-overload","id":1021856,"title":"Scale and Sensory overload","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-24T23:22:19-08:00","id":1021856,"title":"Scale and Sensory overload","content":"How would you handle a sensory overload of a person? For instance, if someone cast web of life without detailing specifically what kind of creatures they were trying to sense - or if they did a similar effect to sense all the minds within an area? Or who cast a spell to get a mental blueprint of an entire neighborhood - including all buildings, vehicles, objects, and people/things within that area?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T23:33:02-08:00","id":1021860,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't. Knowing spells, which you're describing, are non-sensory.<br /> You simply know what you desire, no need to mentally scan over every piece of information.<br /> Cast a cataloguing spell on a library? You know every book in it, with no need to mentally run over every cover.<br /> You can't be overloaded by the mere knowledge of all the life nearby. Blown away? Perhaps. But not overloaded.<br /> Because there's nothing to overload, bar your sense of proportion.<br /> <br /> Unveiling though, which let you see something beyond perception? Those could potentially inflict the Blind condition temporarily if you've unveiled your sight, and stared straight into a metaphorical supernova.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T05:11:34-08:00","id":1021947,"title":"","content":"A custom Conflict that inflicts a -1 penalty to Mental actions, that is non-Persistent and may be resolved earlier if the mage takes time to sort out the info without using magic to do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T08:04:14-08:00","id":1021983,"title":"","content":"I'd just use a Tilt until such time as they drop the spell. If the spell is set to run a long time then convert it into a Condition that can generate Beats as appropriate because a Mage would totally do that to themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T18:39:54-08:00","id":1023060,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12644_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12644\" data-vbnamecard=\"12644\">HerbertIsBestBert</a> Well you can have an information overload :-p But specifically I referenced sensory overload since the spell web of life (a knowing spell) actually says that it might cause a sensory overload if you don't specify what kind of life your sensing.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12619_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12619\" data-vbnamecard=\"12619\">21C Hermit</a> Hm... ok. Or Maybe model it similar to mage sight, to provide penalties to actions unrelated to the spell?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> Yeah I can see that. Or casting it on someone else to overload them. <br /> <br /> Thanks for the replies <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}